  "summary": "Four studies directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling (Bayesian hierarchical models) to early prediction of septic deterioration. [V0017] (El-Sayed et al., 2022) evaluates this method on the Atlas-ICU dataset, reporting AUROC of 0.69. [V0019] (Gupta et al., 2024) applies the same method to the LedgerGuard dataset, achieving accuracy of 0.83. [V0018] (Fischer et al., 2023) reports F1 of 0.76 on AgriSat-4. [V0020] (Haddad et al., 2025) applies the method to CellLife, reporting MAE of 0.90. A fifth candidate, [V0012] (Fischer et al., 2023), applies decentralised training without pooled records—not Bayesian hierarchical models—to sepsis prediction on CellLife (F1=0.68), making it only partially relevant. Documents that merely mention Bayesian hierarchical sepsis work in passing (e.g., [V0177], [V0111], [V0088], [V0193]) are excluded as prior-work mentions, not direct applications.",
